  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1223 PM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nIncreased moisture sticks around in the lower and middle levels \nFriday through the weekend drifting towards South Texas as mid-level \nridging builds over the Southern and Central Plains through early \nnext week. The pattern becomes a bit more disorganized/uncertain \nheading into the middle of next week with a possible inverted trough \nor shortwave moving towards the area.\n\nRain chances are seen Friday into next week though locations may \nvary day to day with no notable upper level support. The Coastal \nPlains will consistently have the better chances due to any \nseabreeze activity in the afternoon and evenings. Temperatures \nremain relatively steady this weekend into next week from the low \n90s to around 100 degrees. Heat index values will generally be from \n102 to 108 degrees, highest in the Coastal Plains and along the I-35 \ncorridor where higher moisture resides. Lows remain in the 70s with \npossibly some increased cloudiness as we head towards the middle of \nnext week.",
